course: dictionary
lesson: 7683
title: Protective and what it tells you
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A word can tell you what something is for. «Protective gloves» are gloves made to keep your hands safe from harm. Look at the words around the word to find its meaning, and check by swapping in your own meaning.
explain: The same word can describe a person. «Mum is very protective of the baby» means she wants to keep the baby safe. Sometimes she may worry too much, so protective can be a kind thing or a little too much.
explain: Sentences that describe animals and people help you too. «Cows with calves can be very protective and can trample people» shows that protective is about guarding someone. «Big sisters are often bossy and protective in the same morning» shows that protective can be a good feeling and an annoying one at the same time.
fact: Protective is an adjective: protective, more protective, most protective.
fact: «Protective» means made to keep someone or something safe from harm, like protective goggles or protective helmets.
fact: «Protective» can also mean wanting to keep someone safe, sometimes too much.
fact: Useful phrases are protective clothing, protective gear, protective layer, and protective of someone.
fact: Louise Bourgeois made giant spider sculptures called «Maman», French for mummy, and she said the spider stood for her mother, who was protective and patient.
exercise: «In science lessons pupils wear protective goggles.» What do protective goggles do? | They help you read faster | *They keep your eyes safe from harm | They make your eyes look bigger | They make it harder to see
exercise: «Big sisters are often bossy and protective in the same morning.» What does protective mean here? | Lost and alone | Angry at everyone | Tired and hungry | *Wanting to keep someone safe, sometimes too much
exercise: «A squash ball is small enough to fit into the eye socket, so protective eyewear is recommended.» What is protective eyewear for? | Making your hair look nice | *Keeping your eyes safe from harm | Reading in the dark | Keeping your feet warm
test: «Cows with calves can be very protective.» What does protective mean here? | *Guarding their young to keep them safe | Hungry for grass | Shy and quiet | Kind and gentle
test: Which word fits the gap? "Players wear protective ___ and pads in sport." | feathers | sandwiches | *helmets
exam: Which word means made to keep someone or something safe from harm? | Loud | Careless | Sticky | *Protective
